description:
## Why

After PKIX-amgn.2 lands `pkix-profiles-cabf`, the original `pkix-profiles` crate keeps only:

1. The `Profile` trait, `ValidationPolicy` struct, framework helpers (`sc081_validity_cap` and similar move OUT).
2. `BasicSmimeProfile` — RFC 8551 §3 baseline only.
3. `BasicTlsProfile` — RFC 5280 + RFC 6125 + universally-required `id-kp-serverAuth` EKU.

This is a **breaking change** for downstream consumers of `TlsBrProfile` / `SmimeProfile`; they will need to add `pkix-profiles-cabf` to their Cargo.toml and update imports.

## What

### BasicSmimeProfile (new)

Implements `Profile` with the RFC 8551 §3 mandatory cert-profile bits:

```rust
pub struct BasicSmimeProfile;

impl Profile for BasicSmimeProfile {
    fn policy(&self, _now_unix: u64) -> ValidationPolicy {
        ValidationPolicy {
            required_leaf_eku: Some(OID_ID_KP_EMAIL_PROTECTION),
            require_subject_alt_name: true,
            require_rfc822_san: true,
            // No validity caps, no key-size floors, no policy-OID requirements.
            // Those are CA/B Forum overlay — see pkix-profiles-cabf::SmimeBrProfile.
            ..Default::default()
        }
    }
}
```

### BasicTlsProfile (new)

Implements `Profile` with the universally-applicable TLS server-cert hygiene:

```rust
pub struct BasicTlsProfile;

impl Profile for BasicTlsProfile {
    fn policy(&self, _now_unix: u64) -> ValidationPolicy {
        ValidationPolicy {
            required_leaf_eku: Some(OID_ID_KP_SERVER_AUTH),
            require_subject_alt_name: true,
            // RFC 6125 hostname matching is on by default in pkix-path; nothing
            // extra needed here. No validity caps, no key-size floors — those
            // are CA/B Forum overlay (pkix-profiles-cabf::TlsBrProfile).
            ..Default::default()
        }
    }
}
```

### Strip from pkix-profiles

- `SmimeProfile` (Mailbox-validated / strict) — moves to `pkix-profiles-cabf::SmimeBrProfile` (composed atop `BasicSmimeProfile` + CA/B Forum overlay).
- `TlsBrProfile` — moves to `pkix-profiles-cabf::TlsBrProfile`.
- `sc081_validity_cap()` and any other ballot-keyed helpers — move to `pkix-profiles-cabf`.
- `SC081_VALIDITY_CAP_DAYS` and similar constants — move.

### Stay in pkix-profiles

- `Profile` trait.
- `ValidationPolicy` struct.
- Anything that composes profiles (`combine_profiles`, etc., if any).
- Generic helpers that are framework-shaped.

## Acceptance

- [ ] `BasicSmimeProfile` + `BasicTlsProfile` implemented with RFC-baseline ValidationPolicy.
- [ ] No `Tls` or `Smime` types with CA/B Forum-specific fields remain in pkix-profiles.
- [ ] cargo check + tests clean across workspace.
- [ ] Crate version bumped to next major (breaking change).
- [ ] CHANGELOG entry documenting the migration.

## Depends on

PKIX-amgn.1 (stance anchor), PKIX-amgn.2 (target crate for moved content).
